% Minimal first-order fixture: universal instantiation.
%
% Ground truth for the first-order work.  Everything here is passed straight
% through to Fellowship, so this script exercises the prover's first-order path
% without depending on the wrapper's proof-term parser.  The `start argument`
% form of the same proof is added once the parser understands ConsFO.
%
% Expected proof term at qed:
%   ;:thesis:P O.<;:th:P O.<ax||O*th>||thesis>
% where `O*th` is ConsFO -- a first-order instantiation, not a propositional
% Cons.  Note `focus ax th.` is deliberately spelled out as `cut` + `axiom`:
% `focus` aborts the prover on a first-order goal.  See tasks.org,
% aida-fellowship-focus-firstorder-crash.

lj.
minimal.

declare N: type.
declare O: N.
declare P: N -> bool.
declare ax: (forall n:N, P [n]).

theorem fo_forall: (P [O]).
prove fo_forall.
cut (forall n:N, P [n]) th.
axiom ax.
elim [O].
axiom.
qed.
